.PP 
.SS "void csmp::TemperatureDensityPressure_Example::Run ()\fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP

.PP
Computation of a hydrostatic (pore) pressure profile in a sedimentary basin\&.

.PP
Illustration of how to use CSMP for one-dimensional models\&. Illustration of how to use the fluid equation of state (EOS) module\&.

.PP
Steps:

.PP
.IP "1." 4
First a vertical (1D) temperature profile is computed\&. This can be done in a single step because it is essentially independent on fluid density\&.
.IP "2." 4
Using an initial guess of the water density of 1000 kg/m3 an iterative process is started where rho(p,T) is adjusted incrementally using the new pressure estimates\&. If no further change occurs (within a given tolerance), the (Picard) iteration is stopped\&.
.PP

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
Use Maple or Excel to visualize '\fI\&.mpl' and '\fP\&.txt' output files, respectively\&. 
.RE
